/P 458 0 R
/E (The perspectives in this section examine the trust architecture required to support that shift. Together, they show that institutional readiness is built through more than policy ambition. It depends on the systems that connect the rule to the regulated: compliance intelligence, security, traceability, monitoring, and the operational ability to prove trust in practice.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
783 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 458 0 R
/E (As digital finance moves from experimentation to institutional deployment, regulation is no longer a peripheral consideration. It is becoming a core layer of financial infrastructure. The ability of digital assets, tokenized markets, and programmable financial systems to scale depends not only on innovation, but on whether they can operate within frameworks that provide legal clarity, operational discipline, and trusted market participation.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
