/E (Executive Summary)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
810 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 459 0 R
/E (The digital asset ecosystem is undergoing a structural transition from regulatory ambiguity to institutionally aligned compliance frameworks. Jurisdictions that prioritise clarity, governance and risk-based supervision are enabling scalable financial use cases across payments, markets and treasury operations. The Abu Dhabi Global Market \(ADGM\) stands out as a leading example of this approach. As the sector evolves toward Central Bank-backed stablecoins, commonly referred to as Central Bank Digital Currencies \(CBDCs\), robust regulatory infrastructure will be critical to ensuring trust, interoperability and systemic resilience.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
811 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 459 0 R
/E (Introduction)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
812 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 459 0 R
/E (Over the past decade, the digital asset ecosystem has evolved from a largely unregulated, experimental environment into an increasingly structured and institutionally relevant financial domain. What began as a technology-led movement centred on decentralisation is now entering a phase defined by regulatory clarity, compliance discipline and integration with traditional financial systems.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
813 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 459 0 R
/E (At the heart of this transition lies a fundamental shift: regulatory compliance is no longer viewed as a constraint on innovation, but as a prerequisite for scale. Early-stage market development was driven by technological capability; the next phase is being shaped by regulatory credibility.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
814 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 459 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
815 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 459 0 R
/E (Among these, the Abu Dhabi Global Market \(ADGM\) has emerged as a leading example of how a forward-looking regulatory framework can enable responsible innovation while maintaining market integrity.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
816 0 obj
<<
