/E (Data and cloud sovereignty are often seen as sources of business friction. In the UAE, they are being used to provide structure and predictability. The current status of the personal data export obligations under Federal Personal Data Protection Law means that there is greater flexibility compared to many markets around the cross-border transfer of personal data. And in its financial free zones, where the UAE has standalone and mature data protection frameworks, we see clarity and progressive features embedded in the law to ensure the compliance burden proportionate and manageable-,)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [61]
