1041 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 463 0 R
/E (The UAE will face its FATF fifth round mutual evaluation in 2026. This is not a formality. The new methodology places decisive weight on demonstrated outcomes: enforcement results, beneficial ownership transparency, virtual asset oversight and cross-border cooperation. Rules on paper are no longer enough. This evaluation arrives at a defining moment. The UAE took over the presidency of MENAFATF in January 2026. The CBUAE has approved its first dirham backed stablecoins. VARA has updated all twelve of its rulebooks. The DIFC hosts close to 1,700 AI and FinTech organisations. These are extraordinary achievements. But they raise the stakes. A jurisdiction that positions itself as the intelligent core of global digital finance needs to show that its compliance infrastructure operates with the same sophistication as its regulatory ambition.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
