/E (Financial infrastructure is no longer merely a utility for moving money. It is becoming an intelligent architecture that transmits value, information, trust, and market signals across jurisdictions, institutions, and asset classes. In this new paradigm, it functions much like a neural network: payments act as sensory inputs, capital allocation interprets and routes signals, and secondary markets generate feedback that strengthens the resilience of the overall system.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [13]
>>
