1517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (The institutions that will define the next phase of this market are those combining deep digital asset expertise with strong regulatory compliance and, crucially, infrastructure that is purpose-built for institutional operations. Trust will be the defining factor. In a market where stablecoin settlements reached $9 trillion globally in 2025, the stakes are too high and the volumes too large for anything less than institutional-grade security, governance, and operational resilience.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
1518 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (The UAE has laid the foundation. The regulatory frameworks are live. The institutional infrastructure is scaling. And the global attention this market is attracting, from sovereign wealth funds, central banks, and multinational financial institutions, confirms that what is happening here is not a regional experiment but a model for how digital asset adoption can work at a national level.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
1519 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (The opportunity is real, but so is the responsibility. For institutions considering their next move, the question is how to strategically build the infrastructure that makes engagement sustainable, compliant, and scalable. The UAE is demonstrating what that looks like in practice, and the institutions stepping forward today will shape how this market develops for decades to come.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
1520 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (We are no longer debating whether digital assets belong in institutional finance. The question now is how strategically institutions deploy the infrastructure to support them, and which jurisdictions have created the conditions for that deployment to succeed at scale.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
1521 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (From my vantage point leading banking strategy at Fireblocks, working daily with financial institutions navigating this transition, the UAE stands out. Not because of aspiration or rhetoric, but because of operational reality. The regulatory architecture is in place. The institutional appetite is proven. And the infrastructure layer, the connective tissue that turns policy into practice, is maturing faster here than in almost any other market.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
