/E (In December 2025, Circle Internet Group was granted Financial Services Permission by the Abu Dhabi Global Market \(ADGM\) to operate as a money services provider. As the UAE sets itself as a leader in stablecoin innovation, this begs the question whether there have been historical examples of other centres driving financial innovation. We believe the development of the Eurodollar in the 1950s-60s is one such example. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1552 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 474 0 R
/E (It started in the Midlands)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1553 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 474 0 R
/E (1955, like today, was a period of significant interest rate movements, with the Bank of England rate reaching a post-war high of 4.5%. Deposit rates were low, Gilt rates were high, so clearing banks like Midland sought to attract dollar funding. The dollars came from Marshall Plan funds in European commercial and central banks as well as the US balance of payments deficit, given extra impetus by Regulation Q in the US, which capped deposit interest rates. Midland converted the dollars into sterling in the FX forward market and lent the proceeds to its clients, a model that quickly spread.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
1554 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 474 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
