/P 478 0 R
/E (Digital asset companies operate complex technological systems while safeguarding significant volumes of digital assets on behalf of clients. In doing so, they face a range of potential exposures, including cyber incidents, internal fraud, operational errors, and loss of digital assets due to third-party crime.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
1736 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 478 0 R
/E (Insurance allows companies to transfer part of these risks to insurers with strong financial capacity. By converting unpredictable losses into manageable and predictable costs, insurance enables firms to focus on innovation and expansion rather than maintaining large reserves against rare but severe events.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
1737 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 478 0 R
/T (When a digital asset platform carries coverage such as directors and officers liability or professional indemnity, it signals that the organisation has undergone independent risk evaluation and meets the underwriting standards required by insurers. This external validation can help reassure investors, counterparties, and clients that a platform operates with appropriate safeguards.)
/E (When a digital asset platform carries coverage such as directors and officers liability or professional indemnity, it signals that the organisation has undergone independent risk evaluation and meets the underwriting standards required by insurers. This external validation can help reassure investors, counterparties, and clients that a platform operates with appropriate safeguards.)
