/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 479 0 R
/E (The global financial system is entering a new architectural phase. Digital assets, tokenized assets, and programmable financial infrastructure are expanding rapidly. According to the 2025 Skynet Digital Asset Treasuries \(DAT\) Report, public companies now hold more than $130 billion in digital assets, highlighting the growing role of institutional capital in digital financial markets. As this trend continues to expand, the most important innovation may not be a new financial product or trading venue; it may be the infrastructure that quietly holds these systems together. )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [9 2111 0 R 11]
>>
endobj
1766 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Span
/K [10]
/Pg 39 0 R
/P 2111 0 R
>>
endobj
1767 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 479 0 R
/E (Increasingly, that infrastructure functions as intelligence. In traditional finance, stability relies on regulation, capital buffers, and institutional oversight. Digital finance introduces another requirement: the ability to see risk as it develops across a distributed, technology-driven ecosystem. )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1768 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 479 0 R
/E (Across the Middle East, particularly in the United Arab Emirates, policymakers and institutions are beginning to recognize this shift. Visibility is becoming as important as capital. )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
