/K [15]
>>
endobj
1771 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 479 0 R
/E (Over the past several years, the UAE has positioned itself as one of the most forward-looking jurisdictions for digital finance. Abu Dhabi Global Market \(ADGM\) introduced one of the earliest comprehensive regulatory frameworks for digital assets in 2018, and Dubai later established the Virtual Assets Regulatory Authority \(VARA\), creating a dedicated licensing regime for Web3 companies. )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
1772 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 479 0 R
/E (These frameworks have helped attract exchanges, infrastructure providers, and blockchain developers to the region. For many companies, the UAE functions not only as a regional hub but as a bridge to global markets, offering )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
1773 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 479 0 R
/E (regulatory clarity while supporting expansion into Asia and Europe. )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
1774 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 479 0 R
/E (Institutional capital has also played a significant role. Sovereign wealth funds and regional investment institutions are exploring blockchain infrastructure, tokenization, and digital asset markets as part of broader economic diversification strategies. )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
1775 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 479 0 R
/E (This combination of regulatory innovation, capital, and global positioning has made the UAE one of the most active digital finance ecosystems today. Rapid innovation, however, introduces a new challenge: visibility. )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
1776 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 479 0 R
/E (The Growing Challenge of Risk Visibility)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
1777 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 479 0 R
/E (Digital asset ecosystems operate very differently from traditional financial markets. A single platform may involve smart contracts running on public blockchains, backend infrastructure hosted across several jurisdictions, and users interacting through multiple exchanges and liquidity pools. )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
1778 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 479 0 R
/E (Risk signals are therefore distributed across networks rather than concentrated within a single institution. A vulnerability in one smart contract can cascade across interconnected protocols. Liquidity shocks may propagate quickly across chains. Security incidents can unfold in minutes rather than days. As CertiK revealed in the 2025 Skynet Hack3D Web3 Security Report, the Web3 sector experienced 630 security incidents in 2025, resulting in total losses of approximately $3.35 billion. )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [23 2112 0 R 25]
>>
endobj
1779 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Span
/K [24]
/Pg 39 0 R
/P 2112 0 R
>>
endobj
1780 0 obj
<<
