1787 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 479 0 R
/E (In this emerging architecture, infrastructure providers are becoming an essential intelligence layer within digital markets. Platforms that monitor blockchain activity and analyze smart contract security generate signals that help institutions and regulators detect vulnerabilities early. When these signals are aggregated across ecosystems, they provide a clearer understanding of how risk may propagate through interconnected networks. )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [33]
>>
endobj
1788 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 479 0 R
/E (For institutional participants, this visibility is critical. Banks, sovereign funds, and asset managers require rigorous security standards and operational transparency comparable to those of traditional financial markets. Technologies such as CertiK's formal verification help provide mathematically provable guarantees about the correctness of critical protocols, building the trust necessary to bridge the gap between the experimental origins of Web3 and the expectations of institutional finance.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [34]
>>
endobj
1789 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 479 0 R
/E (Across the Middle East, collaborations between infrastructure providers and regulators are beginning to support this transition. At CertiK, we have established operations in Abu Dhabi and are working with regional stakeholders to deploy monitoring infrastructure. For instance, our platform Skynet Enterprise aggregates security scores, risk indicators, and compliance signals across organizations. )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [35]
>>
